  half 2 (PODIUM_RUNTIME_DRIVER=generic-pty demotes it): PARTIAL — measured,
  but not to the row's full wording, and the reason is POD-2853.
  On this rig the terminal arm was driven (drive-up.sh with P2777_DRIVER=
  generic-pty; drive-verify.sh read generic-pty back out of the RUNNING
  daemon's /proc/<pid>/environ, so the arm is the daemon's, not a script's
  intention). Under it the session did NOT bind a server driver — it took
  the abduco path and died there:
      status=exited  exitCode=-1  driverId=(none)
      spawnFailure="…/bin/abduco exited 1: create-session: File name too long"
      label=podium-p2777-2591ded6-bfe5-42d7-965b-80d99fd9916f
  The escape hatch DID demote — abduco is the terminal path and a server
  driver would never have touched it. What cannot be read is the demoted
  session's reported driver identity, because the session does not survive
  long enough to report one. PASS on "demotes", unread on "and reports it".

